---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const pageTitle = "Unit 6: Recursion";
const unit = "Unit 6";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  unit={unit}
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">
    {pageTitle}
  </h1>
  <hr class="mb-6" />

  <!-- Learning Outcomes -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
    >
      Learning Outcomes
    </summary>

    <ul class="list-disc ml-6 mt-2">
      <li>Define recursion</li>
      <li>
        Inspect recursive programs
      </li>
      <li>Create recursive programs</li>
      <li>
        Differentiate recursive vs
        iterative solutions
      </li>
      <li>
        Estimate time complexity of
        recursive programs
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-3">
      <b>Key Focus:</b> Base case, recursive
      case, termination, and recurrence relations.
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- Concept Overview -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
    >
      What is Recursion?
    </summary>

    <p>
      Recursion is a technique where a
      function calls itself to solve
      smaller subproblems.
    </p>

    <ul class="list-disc ml-6 mt-2">
      <li>
        <b>Base Case:</b> Stops recursion
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Recursive Case:</b> Reduces problem
        size
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-3">
      <b>Exam Insight:</b> Every recursive
      solution must shrink toward a base case.
    </p>
  </details>

  <!-- Decimal to Binary -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
    >
      Decimal to Binary (Recursion)
    </summary>

    <p>
      Divide by 2 until zero. Print
      remainders in reverse.
    </p>

    <h4 class="font-semibold mt-3">
      C Implementation
    </h4>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-c">
{`
#include <stdio.h>

void decibinary(int num) {
    if (num < 2) {
        printf("%d", num);
    } else {
        decibinary(num / 2);
        printf("%d", num % 2);
    }
}
`}
</code></pre>

    <h4 class="font-semibold mt-3">
      Java Implementation
    </h4>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-java">
{`
public class DecimalToBinary {

    public static void decibinary(int num) {
        if (num < 2) {
            System.out.print(num);
        } else {
            decibinary(num / 2);
            System.out.print(num % 2);
        }
    }
}
`}
</code></pre>
  </details>

  <!-- Reverse String -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
    >
      Print String in Reverse
    </summary>

    <h4 class="font-semibold mt-3">
      C Implementation
    </h4>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-c">
{`
#include <stdio.h>

void print_reverse(char ss[], int n) {
    if (n == 1) {
        printf("%c", ss[0]);
    } else {
        printf("%c", ss[n-1]);
        print_reverse(ss, n-1);
    }
}
`}
</code></pre>

    <h4 class="font-semibold mt-3">
      Java Implementation
    </h4>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-java">
{`
public class ReverseString {

    public static void printReverse(String s) {
        if (s.length() == 1) {
            System.out.print(s);
        } else {
            System.out.print(s.charAt(s.length() - 1));
            printReverse(s.substring(0, s.length() - 1));
        }
    }
}
`}
</code></pre>
  </details>

  <!-- Palindrome -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
    >
      Palindrome Check
    </summary>

    <h4 class="font-semibold mt-3">
      C Implementation
    </h4>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-c">
{`
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int check(char str[], int len) {
    if (len <= 1)
        return 1;

    if (str[0] == str[len - 1] &&
        check(str + 1, len - 2))
        return 1;

    return 0;
}
`}
</code></pre>

    <h4 class="font-semibold mt-3">
      Java Implementation
    </h4>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-java">
{`
public class Palindrome {

    public static boolean check(String s) {
        if (s.length() <= 1)
            return true;

        if (s.charAt(0) == s.charAt(s.length() - 1))
            return check(s.substring(1, s.length() - 1));

        return false;
    }
}
`}
</code></pre>
  </details>

  <!-- GCD -->
  <details
    class="mb-4 border rounded p-4"
  >
    <summary
      class="cursor-pointer font-semibold"
    >
      Greatest Common Divisor (Euclid)
    </summary>

    <h4 class="font-semibold mt-3">
      C Implementation
    </h4>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-c">
{`
int gcd(int p, int q) {
    if (q == 0)
        return p;
    return gcd(q, p % q);
}
`}
</code></pre>

    <h4 class="font-semibold mt-3">
      Java Implementation
    </h4>
    <pre
      class="bg-gray-100 p-2 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code class="language-java">
{`
public class Euclid {

    public static int gcd(int p, int q) {
        if (q == 0)
            return p;
        return gcd(q, p % q);
    }

    public static int gcdIterative(int p, int q) {
        while (q != 0) {
            int temp = q;
            q = p % q;
            p = temp;
        }
        return p;
    }
}
`}
</code></pre>

    <p class="mt-2">
      <b>Key Identity:</b>
      gcd(p, q) = gcd(q, p % q)
    </p>
  </details>

